{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q416791","formula":"C₁₉H₂₁NO","hill":"C19H21NO","elements":["H","C","N","O"],"composition":{"C":19.0,"H":21.0,"N":1.0,"O":1.0},"names":{"en":"Cidoxepin","ru":"Доксепин","uk":"Доксепін"},"descriptions":{"en":"Cidoxepin (former developmental code name P-4599), also known as cis-doxepin or (Z)-doxepin, is a tricyclic antidepressant which was developed in the 1960s but was never marketed. It is the cis or (Z) stereoisomer of doxepin, a mixture of (E) and (Z) isomers that is used commercially in a ratio of approximately 17:3 with cidoxepin as a relatively minor constituent. However, the drug has similar activity to that of doxepin, acting as a serotonin–norepinephrine reuptake inhibitor, H1 receptor antagonist, and anticholinergic, and notably is thought to have more antidepressant activity than trans-doxepin."},"fame":4,"pubchemCid":667468,"mass":279.4,"charge":0,"smiles":"CN(C)CC/C=C\\1/C2=CC=CC=C2COC3=CC=CC=C31","inchikey":"ODQWQRRAPPTVAG-BOPFTXTBSA-N","iupac":"(3Z)-3-(6H-benzo[c][1]benzoxepin-11-ylidene)-N,N-dimethylpropan-1-amine","classes":[{"qid":"Q113145171","names":{"en":"type of chemical entity","ru":"тип химического объекта","uk":"тип хімічної сутності"}}],"structureInfo":{"kind":"molecule","source":"pubchem","ref":"667468","atoms":42,"license":"PubChem (NIH), public data"},"structure":{"kind":"molecule","atoms":[{"x":-1.335,"y":1.421,"z":-1.605,"el":"O"},{"x":4.449,"y":-1.122,"z":-0.496,"el":"N"},{"x":-0.325,"y":-0.381,"z":0.309,"el":"C"},{"x":-1.701,"y":-0.949,"z":0.216,"el":"C"},{"x":-0.026,"y":1.067,"z":0.375,"el":"C"},{"x":-2.752,"y":-0.276,"z":-0.447,"el":"C"},{"x":2.159,"y":-0.728,"z":0.283,"el":"C"},{"x":0.742,"y":-1.199,"z":0.204,"el":"C"},{"x":3.075,"y":-1.606,"z":-0.568,"el":"C"},{"x":-2.629,"y":1.094,"z":-1.086,"el":"C"},{"x":-0.542,"y":1.922,"z":-0.605,"el":"C"},{"x":-1.988,"y":-2.178,"z":0.85,"el":"C"},{"x":-4.036,"y":-0.859,"z":-0.467,"el":"C"},{"x":0.778,"y":1.614,"z":1.384,"el":"C"},{"x":-0.228,"y":3.282,"z":-